Weekly Schedule
Unit 1: Foundations of Programming & Python Syntax

Week 1: Introduction to Python & Environment Setup
Overview of programming languages and Python’s history/use cases.
Installing Python, VS Code / PyCharm, and working with the interactive shell (IDLE).
Writing your first Python script (Hello, World!).

Week 2: Variables, Data Types, and Operators
Understanding variables, naming conventions, and memory assignment.
Basic data types: Integers, Floats, Strings, and Booleans.
Arithmetic, assignment, and comparison operators.

Week 3: Conditional Statements (Control Flow)
Making decisions in code: if, elif, and else statements.
Nested conditionals and logical operators (and, or, not).
Practical logic building: Grade calculators or simple interactive games.

Week 4: Loops & Iteration (While & For Loops)
Repetitive tasks using while loops and infinite loop prevention.
Iterating through sequences using for loops and the range() function.
Loop control statements: break, continue, and pass.

Unit 2: Data Structures & Modular Programming

Week 5: Strings & Basic String Manipulation
String indexing, slicing, and immutability.
Built-in string methods (upper(), lower(), strip(), replace(), split()).\
Basic string formatting (f-strings).

Week 6: Lists & Tuples
Introduction to collections: Lists (mutable) vs. Tuples (immutable).
List methods: append(), insert(), remove(), sort(), and slicing.
Iterating through lists and basic list comprehensions.

Week 7: Dictionaries & Sets
Key-value pairs using Dictionaries (dict) and dictionary methods.
Unordered unique collections using Sets.
Choosing the right data structure for specific problems.

Week 8: Functions & Modular Code
Defining and calling functions with def.
Parameters, arguments, default values, and keyword arguments.
The return statement and understanding variable scope (Local vs. Global).
Mid-Term Project / Review Week

Unit 3: Advanced Concepts & Error Handling

Week 9: Error & Exception Handling
Syntax errors vs. Runtime errors (Exceptions).
Using try, except, else, and finally blocks.
Raising custom exceptions.

Week 10: File Handling (I/O)
Opening, reading, writing, and closing text files (open(), read(), write()).
Using the with context manager for safe file operations.
Working with CSV files using Python's built-in csv module.

Week 11: Introduction to Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) - Part 1
Principles of OOP: Classes and Objects.
Defining constructors (__init__) and instance attributes/methods.

Week 12: Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) - Part 2
The four pillars of OOP introduction: Inheritance, Polymorphism, Encapsulation, and Abstraction.
Writing reusable and organized class-based code.

Unit 4: Working with Libraries & Final Capstone
Week 13: Working with Modules and Standard Libraries
Importing modules (import, from ... import).
Exploring built-in utility libraries: math, random, datetime, and os.
Installing third-party packages using pip.

Week 14: Introduction to Data Analysis / Automation Basics

Introduction to popular external libraries like NumPy or Pandas (basic data manipulation).
Simple file/folder automation tasks using Python.

Week 15: Final Capstone Project Presentations

Submission and presentation of final student projects.
Code review, debugging practices, and future learning paths (Web dev, Data Science, AI).
